The `longest_sequence` function finds the longest sequence in the sorted array. An empty array is returned if the array has less than two elements. Two lists `longest` and `current` are used to keep track of the longest sequence so far and the current sequence respectively. The function iterates through the array, adding elements to the current sequence if they are sequentially after the last element of the current sequence. If they are not, the current sequence is compared with the longest sequence so far, and the longest sequence is updated if necessary. After the loop, the function checks the length of the longest sequence one last time and then returns it. If the longest sequence only contains one element, an empty array is returned.

