def is_valid_ip(ip_str):
    # Split the IP address into four parts
    parts = ip_str.split('.')

    # Check if there are exactly four parts
    if len(parts) != 4:
        return False

    # Check if each part is a valid number between 0 and 255
    for part in parts:
        if not part.isdigit() or int(part) < 0 or int(part) > 255:
            return False

    return True

HERE IS A JAVASCRIPT CODE THAT USES THE FETCH API TO GET THE CONTENT OF AN URL, WILL REMOVE HTML TAGS, COUNT NUMBER OF WORDS, CONVERT UPPERCASE TO LOWERCASE, AND IDENTIFY ALL UNIQUE WORDS ALONG WITH THEIR FREQUENCY. PLEASE REPLACE 'URL_TO_FETCH' WITH YOUR URL.

```JAVASCRIPT
FETCH('URL_TO_FETCH') 
  .THEN(RESPONSE => {
    IF (RESPONSE.OK) {
      RETURN RESPONSE.TEXT();
    } ELSE {
      THROW NEW ERROR("HTTP ERROR " + RESPONSE.STATUS);  
    }
  })
  .THEN(DATA => {
    // REMOVING HTML TAGS FROM THE CONTENT
    CONST TEXT = DATA.REPLACE(/<[^>]*(>|$)/G, "");

    // CONVERTING ALL UPPERCASE LETTERS TO LOWERCASE
    CONST LOWERCASETEXT = TEXT.TOLOWERCASE();

    // COUNTING NUMBER OF WORDS IN THE TEXT
    CONST WORDS = LOWERCASETEXT.MATCH(/\B\W+\B/G);
    CONST WORDCOUNT = WORDS.LENGTH;
    CONSOLE.LOG(`WORD COUNT: ${WORDCOUNT}`);

    // IDENTIFYING AND PRINTING OUT ALL UNIQUE WORDS AND THEIR FREQUENCY COUNTS
    CONST WORDMAP = WORDS.REDUCE((ACC, WORD) => {
      ACC[WORD] ? ACC[WORD]++ : ACC[WORD] = 1;
      RETURN ACC;
    }, {});

    CONSOLE.LOG('UNIQUE WORDS AND THEIR COUNTS:', WORDMAP);
  })
  .CATCH(ERROR => {
     CONSOLE.LOG('FETCHING CONTENT FAILED', ERROR);
  });
```

REASONING BEHIND THE CODE:
- FETCH API IS USED TO GET THE CONTENT FROM A URL, IT RETURNS A PROMISE THAT RESOLVES TO THE RESPONSE TO THAT REQUEST.
- IF THE RESPONSE IS OKAY IT IS CONVERTED TO TEXT
- A REGULAR EXPRESSION IS USED TO REMOVE HTML TAGS FROM THE TEXT.
- THE TEXT IS THEN CONVERTED TO ALL LOWERCASE.
- THE WORD COUNT IS CALCULATED BY MATCHING WORD CHARACTERS (USING `\W+`) IN THE TEXT.
- FINALLY UNIQUE WORDS ARE FOUND AND THEIR FREQUENCY COUNTS ARE CALCULATED BY REDUCING THE ARRAY OF WORDS (BUILT-IN REDUCE FUNCTION IN JS) INTO AN OBJECT WHERE EACH KEY-VALUE PAIR IS A UNIQUE WORD AND ITS FREQUENCY COUNT. 
- IF SOME ERROR OCCURS DURING FETCHING OF THE CONTENT, IT IS CAUGHT AND PRINTED TO THE CONSOLE.

CONSIDERING TIME AND SPACE COMPLEXITY:
- THE TIME COMPLEXITY IS MAINLY DUE TO THE USE OF THE REDUCE FUNCTION WHICH WOULD REQUIRE O(N) ITERATIONS, WHERE N IS THE NUMBER OF WORDS IN THE `WORDS` ARRAY.
- THE SPACE COMPLEXITY IS ALSO PRIMARILY DEPENDENT ON THE NUMBER OF UNIQUE WORDS IDENTIFIED (MAPPED IN `WORDMAP`), AT WORST CASE N UNIQUE WORDS COULD REQUIRE O(N) SPACE.

